{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtxjpjG2ShqrCZWhX3jy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**decision: changes-requested**\n\nThe lanes themselves work. The problem is that the per-lane metrics R6 requires never reach the operator: `pose runtime status` (JSON or text) doesn't print them. The one measurement run shows this: it recorded `runtime_metrics: null`, and its report has `?` placeholders for those counts. The docs promise those fields in `status`. That's a medium-severity defect, and the policy only accepts low-severity risks, so I can't approve.\n\nI had no shell access (the Bash tool was denied), so I didn't run any tests or tools myself. This review relies on reading the code at `95af7b63` and the sealed evidence.\n\n## What I checked in the code\n\n- **Lanes:** `runtime_lanes.go` keeps its counts consistently. A command is counted when it enters a lane, and on every exit path the count is released, including deadline and shutdown withdrawals (`runtime_host.go:106-127`). `surface-check` goes to the short lane and everything else to the heavy lane, which matches the timings in the spec (about 10 ms against 25 s and 160 s).\n- **Flags:** the numeric flags are bounded and their error messages are clear (`runtime_cmd.go:118-142`). `start` passes them on to the detached `serve` (`runtime_cmd.go:105-108`, `195`).\n- **Thresholds:** T1 0.60, T2 0.80, T3 3× or 250 ms, T4 1536 MiB and T6 500 ms are the same in the test (`runtime_measure_test.go:32-37`), in spec R8 and in the report. The report's `repo_head` is `7c2abbf6`, the commit that added the test and its thresholds. Without git I couldn't confirm that the spec text already had them before that run.\n- **Running commands in parallel in one process:** this is now possible, and the D1 rationale only argues from separate processes. On the plus side, the resident memo is protected by a lock (`resident_git_memo.go:20`) and no hosted path changes the working directory or environment. But the `-race` test only runs `surface-check --help` alongside a heavy check, so the real `surface-check` code path was never race-checked in the same process.\n\n## Findings\n\n| id | sev | where | summary |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 | **medium**, blocker | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go:244` | `runtimeReport` never prints `reply.Metrics`, in either `--json` (`pose.runtime.status/1`) or the text output. R6 and the docs (`POSE.md:947`) say `status` carries `<lane>_*` in `metrics`. Only the Go client API returns them, and that is all the R6 test checks (`runtime_host_test.go:317`). |\n| F2 | low, blocker | `POSE.md:947` (same in `locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:944` and both scaffold copies) | The paragraph still says \"The runtime runs one hosted command at a time\", which contradicts the new lanes text added after it. |\n| F3 | low, blocker | `.pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.md:51` | The \"effective\" line has `?` placeholders, and the JSON has `\"runtime_metrics\": null` (line 81), a symptom of F1. R8 asks the report to say what was effective. |\n| F4 | low, follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:78` | The comment still says commands run \"one at a time… two at once would race themselves\". The safety of parallel runs in one process is still an unverified assumption: no `-race` test covers real short-lane work alongside a heavy check. |\n| F5 | low, follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:139` | `memo_hits` is the difference of a counter shared by the whole process. When commands overlap, one command's count includes cache hits from the others. |\n| F6 | low, follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:210` | T5 says every hosted output equals the standalone one, but only `review-check` is compared. The `surface-check` outputs, idle and under load, are never compared to standalone. |\n| F7 | low, follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:185` | The memory peak for T4 is read before the short-query and concurrent-load phases, so the reported peak leaves those phases out. |\n\n## Criteria\n\n- **Passed:**\n  - **backend-concurrency:** lane counts are balanced; sealed `runtime-qos-integration` (`-race`).\n  - **backend-contracts / compatibility:** `Reply.Metrics` is an additive `omitempty` field, and `status/1` is unchanged.\n  - **backend-input-errors:** the flag bounds hold.\n  - **backend-integration-impact:** the flags reach `serve`.\n  - **design-causality:** two lanes address the 10 ms against 25 s wait the spec measured.\n  - **scope:** the artifacts match the plan.\n  - **security:** no new authority, and the metrics are plain counters.\n  - **solution-proportionality:** a fixed list and two lanes is small. The choice would no longer hold if a short command became slow, or if running commands in parallel in one process caused races.\n- **Finding:**\n  - correctness, requirements, observability, operability: F1.\n  - documentation: F2.\n  - assumption-integrity: F4.\n- **Tools:**\n  - surface-check and both validate runs are answered with the sealed refs.\n  - artifact-check is `deferred`: it names no evidence class, and I couldn't run it without a shell.\n  - review-check and closeout-check are `deferred` until the review is complete.\n  - The recommended tools are `not-used`.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"F1\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"disposition\": \"blocker\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go\", \"line\": 244, \"summary\": \"runtimeReport never emits reply.Metrics in `pose runtime status --json` (pose.runtime.status/1) or in the human output, although R6 and POSE.md:947 say status carries the per-lane metrics; only the Go client API returns them, which is all the R6 test checks (runtime_host_test.go:317). The measurement consequently recorded runtime_metrics null.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"blocker\", \"file\": \"POSE.md\", \"line\": 947, \"summary\": \"The hosted-checks paragraph still states 'The runtime runs one hosted command at a time', contradicting the new lanes text in the same paragraph; same in locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:944 and both scaffold copies.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"blocker\", \"file\": \".pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.md\", \"line\": 51, \"summary\": \"The 'Efetivo' line keeps '?' placeholders for admitted/refused counts and the JSON report has runtime_metrics null (line 81); R8 requires the report to state what was effective.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F4\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go\", \"line\": 78, \"summary\": \"Stale comment says hosted commands run one at a time because two would race; the in-process concurrency safety (D1 argues from separate processes) is only race-tested with `surface-check --help`, not real short-lane work beside a heavy check.\", \"action\": \"Update the comment and add a -race test running a real surface-check concurrently with a heavy check on a fixture project.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F5\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go\", \"line\": 139, \"summary\": \"memo_hits is the delta of a process-global counter; with concurrent lanes a command's reported memo_hits includes other commands' hits.\", \"action\": \"Attribute memo hits per command (context-scoped counter) or document memo_hits as approximate under concurrency.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F6\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go\", \"line\": 210, \"summary\": \"T5 claims every hosted output equals standalone, but surface-check outputs (idle and under heavy load) are never compared with a standalone run.\", \"action\": \"Compare the short-query hosted outputs with a standalone surface-check output in the measurement.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F7\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go\", \"line\": 185, \"summary\": \"T4 reads VmHWM before the short-query and concurrent heavy-load scenarios, so the reported peak excludes the concurrent phase.\", \"action\": \"Read VmHWM at the end of the resident scenarios, before the restart loop.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"}\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F4\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Read runtime_lanes.go and runtime_host.go:106-127: enter/admit/withdrawn/release keep queued and running balanced on every path; the -race integration check runs a heavy and a short command concurrently.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Reply.Metrics is an additive omitempty field; pose.runtime.status/1 and pose.runtime.run/1 are unchanged; runtimeSpawn signature change is internal.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"parseRuntimeFlags (runtime_cmd.go:118-142) bounds each admission flag (slots/memo >=1, queues >=0, <=1048576) with a message naming the flag and range; a full lane refuses with a typed refused outcome.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"start forwards the admission flags to the detached serve via serveArgs (runtime_cmd.go:105-108,195); the fixture spawn path in runtime_host_test.go exercises the same forwarding.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined Reply, Options and the status/run documents: only additive fields and new optional flags; defaults preserve prior behaviour apart from allowing concurrent lanes.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-2c8c4050b1833f7e\", \"rationale\": \"D1 basis R6: the cause (a 10 ms surface-check waiting behind a 25 s review-check under a single semaphore) is removed by a separate short lane; the classification follows the spec's measured timings (roadmap-check heavy).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-2c8c4050b1833f7e\", \"rationale\": \"Compared the change list with the spec's Artifacts: every implementation and doc file is listed; no CPU/cgroup limits or durable queue were added, matching the non-goals.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"No new endpoint or authority; new inputs are bounded integers; metrics are non-sensitive counters; the env-digest and peer checks precede lane admission.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-2c8c4050b1833f7e\", \"rationale\": \"Minimal alternative (one-at-a-time) cannot meet R6; two static lanes with atomics and a channel are ~110 lines with no speculative extension. Invalidated if a short-listed command becomes slow or in-process concurrency races (see F4).\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"No evidence class is named and the reviewer profile had no shell to run it; needs a run by POSE or the implementer.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; no shell available; sealed structure:design-2c8c4050b1833f7e consulted instead.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; no shell available.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; no shell available; sealed integration evidence consulted.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; no shell available.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; no shell available.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"surface-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\"}\n  ]\n}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2408,"cache_read_input_tokens":69833,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2408},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"55d99d5d-a467-461b-93eb-0fc9bcf0fd15","timestamp":"2026-11-10T08:52:17.585Z","request_id":"req_011CgtxjpapiNRiai1uQFj2y"}
{"type":"rate_limit_event","rate_limit_info":{"status":"allowed_warning","resetsAt":1794484800,"rateLimitType":"seven_day","utilization":0.75,"overageStatus":"rejected","overageDisabledReason":"out_of_credits","isUsingOverage":false,"surpassedThreshold":0.75,"unifiedWindows":{"five_hour":{"utilization":0.09,"resetsAt":1794317400,"status":"allowed"},"seven_day":{"utilization":0.75,"resetsAt":1794484800,"status":"allowed_warning","surpassedThreshold":0.75}},"overageEnabled":true},"uuid":"6e4ce995-c3ed-40cb-8919-1113e067cbab","session_id":"[private-session]"}
{"duration_api_ms":150664,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"[private-session]","total_cost_usd":0.9774054000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":28,"cache_creation_input_tokens":66615,"cache_read_input_tokens":633467,"output_tokens":15884,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7476},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":66615,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8005,"cache_read_input_tokens":69833,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2408,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2408},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":28,"outputTokens":15884,"cacheReadInputTokens":633467,"cacheCreationInputTokens":66615,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9774054000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":7476,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":66615,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01D21Q3xakqyppUWPwvbAvTF","tool_input":{"command":"cd pose-mcp && go test -race ./internal/cli -run 'TestAShortQueryIsNotQueuedBehindAHeavyCheck|TestACommandThatNeverStarted|TestRuntime|TestMeasureTheRuntime' -count=1 -v 2>&1 | grep -E '^(=== RUN|--- |PASS|FAIL|ok|.*SKIP)' | head -40; go test -race ./internal/worktreeruntime -count=1 2>&1 | tail -3; cd .. && git status --short | head","timeout":600000,"description":"Run runtime lane and measurement tests with race detector"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":20,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**decision: changes-requested**\n\nThe lanes themselves work. The problem is that the per-lane metrics R6 requires never reach the operator: `pose runtime status` (JSON or text) doesn't print them. The one measurement run shows this: it recorded `runtime_metrics: null`, and its report has `?` placeholders for those counts. The docs promise those fields in `status`. That's a medium-severity defect, and the policy only accepts low-severity risks, so I can't approve.\n\nI had no shell access (the Bash tool was denied), so I didn't run any tests or tools myself. This review relies on reading the code at `95af7b63` and the sealed evidence.\n\n## What I checked in the code\n\n- **Lanes:** `runtime_lanes.go` keeps its counts consistently. A command is counted when it enters a lane, and on every exit path the count is released, including deadline and shutdown withdrawals (`runtime_host.go:106-127`). `surface-check` goes to the short lane and everything else to the heavy lane, which matches the timings in the spec (about 10 ms against 25 s and 160 s).\n- **Flags:** the numeric flags are bounded and their error messages are clear (`runtime_cmd.go:118-142`). `start` passes them on to the detached `serve` (`runtime_cmd.go:105-108`, `195`).\n- **Thresholds:** T1 0.60, T2 0.80, T3 3× or 250 ms, T4 1536 MiB and T6 500 ms are the same in the test (`runtime_measure_test.go:32-37`), in spec R8 and in the report. The report's `repo_head` is `7c2abbf6`, the commit that added the test and its thresholds. Without git I couldn't confirm that the spec text already had them before that run.\n- **Running commands in parallel in one process:** this is now possible, and the D1 rationale only argues from separate processes. On the plus side, the resident memo is protected by a lock (`resident_git_memo.go:20`) and no hosted path changes the working directory or environment. But the `-race` test only runs `surface-check --help` alongside a heavy check, so the real `surface-check` code path was never race-checked in the same process.\n\n## Findings\n\n| id | sev | where | summary |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 | **medium**, blocker | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go:244` | `runtimeReport` never prints `reply.Metrics`, in either `--json` (`pose.runtime.status/1`) or the text output. R6 and the docs (`POSE.md:947`) say `status` carries `<lane>_*` in `metrics`. Only the Go client API returns them, and that is all the R6 test checks (`runtime_host_test.go:317`). |\n| F2 | low, blocker | `POSE.md:947` (same in `locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:944` and both scaffold copies) | The paragraph still says \"The runtime runs one hosted command at a time\", which contradicts the new lanes text added after it. |\n| F3 | low, blocker | `.pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.md:51` | The \"effective\" line has `?` placeholders, and the JSON has `\"runtime_metrics\": null` (line 81), a symptom of F1. R8 asks the report to say what was effective. |\n| F4 | low, follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:78` | The comment still says commands run \"one at a time… two at once would race themselves\". The safety of parallel runs in one process is still an unverified assumption: no `-race` test covers real short-lane work alongside a heavy check. |\n| F5 | low, follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:139` | `memo_hits` is the difference of a counter shared by the whole process. When commands overlap, one command's count includes cache hits from the others. |\n| F6 | low, follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:210` | T5 says every hosted output equals the standalone one, but only `review-check` is compared. The `surface-check` outputs, idle and under load, are never compared to standalone. |\n| F7 | low, follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:185` | The memory peak for T4 is read before the short-query and concurrent-load phases, so the reported peak leaves those phases out. |\n\n## Criteria\n\n- **Passed:**\n  - **backend-concurrency:** lane counts are balanced; sealed `runtime-qos-integration` (`-race`).\n  - **backend-contracts / compatibility:** `Reply.Metrics` is an additive `omitempty` field, and `status/1` is unchanged.\n  - **backend-input-errors:** the flag bounds hold.\n  - **backend-integration-impact:** the flags reach `serve`.\n  - **design-causality:** two lanes address the 10 ms against 25 s wait the spec measured.\n  - **scope:** the artifacts match the plan.\n  - **security:** no new authority, and the metrics are plain counters.\n  - **solution-proportionality:** a fixed list and two lanes is small. The choice would no longer hold if a short command became slow, or if running commands in parallel in one process caused races.\n- **Finding:**\n  - correctness, requirements, observability, operability: F1.\n  - documentation: F2.\n  - assumption-integrity: F4.\n- **Tools:**\n  - surface-check and both validate runs are answered with the sealed refs.\n  - artifact-check is `deferred`: it names no evidence class, and I couldn't run it without a shell.\n  - review-check and closeout-check are `deferred` until the review is complete.\n  - The recommended tools are `not-used`.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"F1\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"disposition\": \"blocker\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go\", \"line\": 244, \"summary\": \"runtimeReport never emits reply.Metrics in `pose runtime status --json` (pose.runtime.status/1) or in the human output, although R6 and POSE.md:947 say status carries the per-lane metrics; only the Go client API returns them, which is all the R6 test checks (runtime_host_test.go:317). The measurement consequently recorded runtime_metrics null.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"blocker\", \"file\": \"POSE.md\", \"line\": 947, \"summary\": \"The hosted-checks paragraph still states 'The runtime runs one hosted command at a time', contradicting the new lanes text in the same paragraph; same in locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:944 and both scaffold copies.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"blocker\", \"file\": \".pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.md\", \"line\": 51, \"summary\": \"The 'Efetivo' line keeps '?' placeholders for admitted/refused counts and the JSON report has runtime_metrics null (line 81); R8 requires the report to state what was effective.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F4\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go\", \"line\": 78, \"summary\": \"Stale comment says hosted commands run one at a time because two would race; the in-process concurrency safety (D1 argues from separate processes) is only race-tested with `surface-check --help`, not real short-lane work beside a heavy check.\", \"action\": \"Update the comment and add a -race test running a real surface-check concurrently with a heavy check on a fixture project.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F5\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go\", \"line\": 139, \"summary\": \"memo_hits is the delta of a process-global counter; with concurrent lanes a command's reported memo_hits includes other commands' hits.\", \"action\": \"Attribute memo hits per command (context-scoped counter) or document memo_hits as approximate under concurrency.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F6\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go\", \"line\": 210, \"summary\": \"T5 claims every hosted output equals standalone, but surface-check outputs (idle and under heavy load) are never compared with a standalone run.\", \"action\": \"Compare the short-query hosted outputs with a standalone surface-check output in the measurement.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F7\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go\", \"line\": 185, \"summary\": \"T4 reads VmHWM before the short-query and concurrent heavy-load scenarios, so the reported peak excludes the concurrent phase.\", \"action\": \"Read VmHWM at the end of the resident scenarios, before the restart loop.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"}\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F4\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Read runtime_lanes.go and runtime_host.go:106-127: enter/admit/withdrawn/release keep queued and running balanced on every path; the -race integration check runs a heavy and a short command concurrently.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Reply.Metrics is an additive omitempty field; pose.runtime.status/1 and pose.runtime.run/1 are unchanged; runtimeSpawn signature change is internal.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"parseRuntimeFlags (runtime_cmd.go:118-142) bounds each admission flag (slots/memo >=1, queues >=0, <=1048576) with a message naming the flag and range; a full lane refuses with a typed refused outcome.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"start forwards the admission flags to the detached serve via serveArgs (runtime_cmd.go:105-108,195); the fixture spawn path in runtime_host_test.go exercises the same forwarding.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined Reply, Options and the status/run documents: only additive fields and new optional flags; defaults preserve prior behaviour apart from allowing concurrent lanes.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-2c8c4050b1833f7e\", \"rationale\": \"D1 basis R6: the cause (a 10 ms surface-check waiting behind a 25 s review-check under a single semaphore) is removed by a separate short lane; the classification follows the spec's measured timings (roadmap-check heavy).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-2c8c4050b1833f7e\", \"rationale\": \"Compared the change list with the spec's Artifacts: every implementation and doc file is listed; no CPU/cgroup limits or durable queue were added, matching the non-goals.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"No new endpoint or authority; new inputs are bounded integers; metrics are non-sensitive counters; the env-digest and peer checks precede lane admission.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-2c8c4050b1833f7e\", \"rationale\": \"Minimal alternative (one-at-a-time) cannot meet R6; two static lanes with atomics and a channel are ~110 lines with no speculative extension. Invalidated if a short-listed command becomes slow or in-process concurrency races (see F4).\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"No evidence class is named and the reviewer profile had no shell to run it; needs a run by POSE or the implementer.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; no shell available; sealed structure:design-2c8c4050b1833f7e consulted instead.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; no shell available.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; no shell available; sealed integration evidence consulted.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; no shell available.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; no shell available.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"surface-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\"}\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":973,"type":"result","duration_ms":151839,"uuid":"c6207c6b-abf6-4456-88f2-20f9f828dad6","ttft_stream_ms":901,"time_to_request_ms":303,"first_content_frame_ms":901,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":28,"outputTokens":15884,"cacheReadInputTokens":633467,"cacheCreationInputTokens":66615,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9774054000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":7476,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":66615,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-04T10:05:09.044Z"}
